## 4. NAGIOS MONITORING

Nagios Core is commonly installed on Ubuntu/Linux. Execute these commands on the Nagios server, not Windows CMD.

### A. Check Nagios status

```bash
sudo systemctl status nagios
```

Start:

```bash
sudo systemctl start nagios
```

Restart:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nagios
```

Enable at startup:

```bash
sudo systemctl enable nagios
```

### B. Open Nagios dashboard

Default web interface:

```text
http://SERVER-IP/nagios
```

Login using configured Nagios web credentials.

### C. Check configuration

```bash
sudo /usr/local/nagios/bin/nagios -v /usr/local/nagios/etc/nagios.cfg
```

Restart after valid configuration changes:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nagios
```

### D. Important Nagios directories

```text
/usr/local/nagios/etc/
/usr/local/nagios/etc/objects/
/usr/local/nagios/libexec/
/usr/local/nagios/var/
```

### E. NRPE monitoring

On the monitored Linux machine, install NRPE and plugins using the package manager appropriate for the Linux distribution.

For Ubuntu/Debian:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nagios-nrpe-server nagios-plugins
```

Check NRPE:

```bash
sudo systemctl status nagios-nrpe-server
```

Restart:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nagios-nrpe-server
```

Default NRPE port: `5666`.

Allow the Nagios server IP in the NRPE configuration, typically:

```text
allowed_hosts=127.0.0.1,NAGIOS_SERVER_IP
```

### F. Example NRPE command

In the monitored host's NRPE configuration:

```text
command[check_root_disk]=/usr/lib/nagios/plugins/check_disk -w 20% -c 10% -p /
```

Plugin path can vary by distribution.

From the Nagios server, test:

```bash
/usr/local/nagios/libexec/check_nrpe -H CLIENT_IP -c check_root_disk
```

Expected output resembles:

```text
DISK OK - free space: ...
```

If command is not defined:
- Check `nrpe.cfg`.
- Verify command name.
- Verify plugin path.
- Restart NRPE.
- Verify port 5666 connectivity.

### G. Useful monitoring commands

```bash
df -h
free -m
uptime
top
systemctl status nagios
systemctl status nagios-nrpe-server
```

