## 5. AWS EC2

### A. Launch an EC2 instance

1. Open AWS Console.
2. Search for EC2.
3. Click Launch Instance.
4. Enter instance name.
5. Select Amazon Linux or Ubuntu AMI.
6. Select instance type.
7. Create/select key pair.
8. Configure Security Group.
9. Launch instance.

### B. Security Group inbound rules

| Type | Port | Source |
|---|---:|---|
| SSH | 22 | My IP |
| HTTP | 80 | 0.0.0.0/0 |
| HTTPS | 443 | 0.0.0.0/0 |
| Custom TCP | 8080 | Appropriate trusted source |

Do not expose SSH to everyone in production.

### C. Connect through SSH

On Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
ssh -i "mykey.pem" ec2-user@PUBLIC_IP
```

For Ubuntu:

```powershell
ssh -i "mykey.pem" ubuntu@PUBLIC_IP
```

If key permissions cause an error in Windows:

```powershell
icacls mykey.pem /inheritance:r
icacls mykey.pem /grant:r "$($env:USERNAME):(R)"
```

### D. Install Apache on Amazon Linux

```bash
sudo dnf update -y
sudo dnf install httpd -y
sudo systemctl start httpd
sudo systemctl enable httpd
```

Create a webpage:

```bash
echo "Welcome to AWS EC2" | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html
```

Access:

```text
http://PUBLIC_IP
```

For Ubuntu, install Apache using:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install apache2 -y
sudo systemctl enable --now apache2
```

### E. Run application on port 8080

Ensure the application listens on an externally reachable interface, such as `0.0.0.0`, and that the Security Group permits TCP 8080.

Check:

```bash
sudo ss -tulnp | grep 8080
```

Access:

```text
http://PUBLIC_IP:8080
```

### F. Persistent storage – EBS

Check disks:

```bash
lsblk
```

Create directory:

```bash
sudo mkdir /data
```

For a new, empty EBS volume only, format it:

```bash
sudo mkfs -t ext4 /dev/DEVICE
```

Mount it:

```bash
sudo mount /dev/DEVICE /data
```

Check:

```bash
df -h
```

Use the correct device name. Never format a volume containing existing data.

### G. AWS important concepts

| Concept | Purpose |
|---|---|
| EC2 | Virtual server |
| AMI | Instance template |
| Key Pair | SSH authentication |
| Security Group | Instance-level virtual firewall |
| EBS | Persistent block storage |
| S3 | Object storage |
| Elastic IP | Static public IPv4 |
| VPC | Isolated virtual network |
| Internet Gateway | Internet connectivity |
| NAT Gateway | Outbound internet for private subnet resources |

