# 6. GIT AND GITHUB – COMMON TO ALL TASKS

### Push a project folder to GitHub

```cmd
cd path\to\project

git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"

git branch -M main

git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git

git push -u origin main
```

If remote already exists:

```cmd
git remote -v
git remote set-url origin https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
git push -u origin main
```

### Update existing project

```cmd
git add .
git commit -m "Updated project"
git push
```

### Useful Git commands

```cmd
git status
git log --oneline
git branch
git remote -v
git pull
```

Never push `.env` files, passwords, private keys or access tokens.

